{
  "profile": "pq_key_binding.v1/cutoff-enforcement",
  "description": "Cutoff enforcement, v1. Admit an artifact iff PROVEN ANCHORED BEFORE the consumer cutoff, OR it carries a VALID PQ companion under the pq_pubkey of the binding IN FORCE at the artifact's anchor time (cutoff by ANCHOR TIME, consumer policy). v1 over v0: (1) the baseline binding governs from creation (activation 0), so an artifact anchored before the baseline's own registration is admitted classical-only rather than retro-invalidated; (2) the verdict is tri-state \u2014 evidence in {verified, refuted, unverifiable}, decision a derived projection. A REVOCATION still ends authority at its anchor time: a post-revocation artifact is REFUTED even pre-cutoff, distinct from an innocent pre-baseline artifact. Each case asserts the resolution step, the evidence, the rule, AND the decision.",
  "v1_changes_from_v0": [
    "pre-baseline artifact: v0 REJECT (no_in_force_binding) -> v1 ADMIT (anchored_before_cutoff); the baseline governs from 0. This is the back-catalogue guarantee zexoverz flagged.",
    "expected.evidence added (verified|refuted|unverifiable); decision is project(evidence).",
    "new case: post-cutoff companion present-but-unchecked -> unverifiable (companion_not_checked), NOT refuted.",
    "UNCHANGED: post-revocation pre-cutoff artifact stays REFUTED / no_in_force_binding (deliberate trust-ending signal, distinct from pre-baseline). This half is Pavlo's revocation lane."
  ],
